Python Libraries Used:

1) gpiozero – For controlling relays via GPIO.

2) lgpio – Alternative GPIO control for stable relay operations.

3) pyserial – If used for debugging or sensor communication over UART.

4) adafruit-ssd1306 – For displaying data on the OLED screen.

5) PIL (Pillow) – For handling graphics on the OLED display.

6) time – Standard library for handling delays and intervals.

7) threading – To run OLED updates and keyboard inputs concurrently.

8) os – If used for system-level operations (not mandatory).




Source Scripts Running on Raspberry Pi

a) Main Python Script

i)   Reads CO₂ data from the K33 ELG sensor via USB.

ii)  Reads temperature from the DS18B20 sensor via 1-Wire GPIO.

iii) Displays real-time data on the SSD1306 OLED screen.

iv)  Controls 5 relays via keyboard input.


b) Additional Scripts

For logging data, a separate script is be running for storage (CSV, SQLite, etc.).


c) External Dependencies

i)  K33 ELG Sensor Communication (Handled via serial over USB).

ii) DS18B20 Sensor (Uses /sys/bus/w1/devices/ in Raspberry Pi OS).

